## 3. Codebase Analysis & Strategic Guidance

The following analysis is based on my direct review of the current codebase. Use these notes and tips to guide your implementation.

### Relevant Existing Code
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/security/IdentityResource.java:1-142`
    *   **Summary:** Placeholder identity/session REST resource that guards every endpoint with `TenantContext` checks and returns structured placeholder responses, illustrating the required logging + context enforcement pattern for security-facing APIs.
    *   **Recommendation:** Mirror this guard pattern in `DataExportResource` (verify context, log tenant ID, short-circuit if context missing) and keep status codes consistent with RFC 7807 payloads instead of ad-hoc JSON bodies.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/security/ProblemDetail.java:1-253`
    *   **Summary:** RFC 7807 helper with builder + canned constructors for 401/403/429 responses, used throughout security modules for consistent error contracts.
    *   **Recommendation:** Use this helper for export/delete failures (e.g., unauthorized, conflict when job already queued, 429 for concurrent requests) so the UI can rely on standardized fields.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/security/BcryptMigrationService.java:1-164`
    *   **Summary:** Demonstrates how security services log sensitive operations, emit Micrometer counters, and encapsulate transactional updates with defensive checks.
    *   **Recommendation:** Follow the same pattern in `DataDeletionJob` when recording purge metrics (e.g., `privacy.export.success`) and when writing audit logs, ensuring tenant-scoped updates happen inside transactional boundaries.
*   **File:** `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/src/views/SettingsView.vue:1-56`
    *   **Summary:** Shows the admin SPA’s design system conventions (Tailwind utility classes, tabbed content, `<script setup>` with TypeScript) and how feature tabs mount child components.
    *   **Recommendation:** Build `AccountSecurityView.vue` using this structural approach—keep layout tokens consistent, leverage stores/components for reusable cards, and wire CTA buttons to API clients generated elsewhere in the SPA.

### Implementation Tips & Notes
*   **Tenancy Enforcement:** `docs/architecture/tenant_isolation.md:120-169` requires that every request populate `TenantContext` before touching data. Reuse the guard from `IdentityResource` and ensure exports/deletions also include tenant metadata in audit records so RLS rules cannot be bypassed.
*   **Export Format:** Blueprint data governance rules (`01_Blueprint_Foundation.md:233-247`) mandate zipped JSONL + CSV manifests stored per-tenant in R2 with short-lived URLs. Design the resource to stage files under tenant-prefixed keys and include manifest JSON describing schema + hash.
*   **Session UX:** The UI spec (`06_UI_UX_Architecture.md:1010-1020` and `06_UI_UX_Architecture.md:1272-1285`) calls for a session list with revoke/report actions plus status messaging for privacy requests. Incorporate these behaviors in `AccountSecurityView.vue`, including education copy and filters.
*   **Runbook Alignment:** Existing runbook sections already mention key rotation monitoring (`docs/operations/runbook.md:540-557`) and GDPR log export workflow (`docs/operations/runbook.md:1848-1885`). Update those sections with the new automation steps, command references, and escalation points so ops has a single truth source.
*   **Async Job Governance:** Background job priorities (`docs/architecture/background_jobs.md:220-260`) place archive exports in BULK and standard report exports in DEFAULT. Choose an appropriate queue for data exports vs deletion purges, emit SLA metrics, and document retries/backoff for long-running pulls.
*   **Storage & Partitions:** Platform ops guidance (`docs/architecture/platform_ops.md:44-74`) highlights R2 tenant prefixes and PostgreSQL session/audit partitions. Ensure deletion jobs clean up both hot partitions and archived blobs, and log manifest metadata for compliance checks.
*   **Error Handling:** `ProblemDetail` plus the security package conventions favor RFC 7807 responses with traceable instances. Include `trace_id`/`job_id` extensions so support teams can reconcile user-facing tickets with background job entries and audit logs.
